  "released": "2026-08-27",
  "changelog": "v235: ADR 0030 — Eras: age frames are the coordinate system, named eras are interpretations (lifehug-platform#686; platform design docs/design/eras.md; viewer parity twin #254). The package half of the Eras / Timeline program's controlling authority: calculated age frames as period nodes, the owner's birth bound to `self` with legacy compatibility and a provisional origin, opaque immutable era identity, era dates only from the person's claims through separate event resolution records, membership and display as separate durable inputs, the atomic `era-record` writer, occurrence scope apart from owner relevance, Play on eras, correction supersession by name, `is_current` as the one classification reader gate. Contracts follow (docs/pr-specs/eras-*.md). AND THE PROMISE v234 MADE IS KEPT: the `mirror_item` read-side alias is deleted — `LEGACY_PLAY_TARGET_KIND` is gone, `PLAY_TARGET_KINDS` is the canonical `work_item` alone, and a stored target still carrying the old word is refused rather than rewritten (`test_the_v227_alias_is_gone`, `test_a_v227_target_no_longer_opens_the_stage`). Zero other executable diff.",
